    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U4", "U24"],
      "pins": ["U4.4", "U4.5", "U24.4", "U24.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U4 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2) are both connected to net GND; U24 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2) are both connected to net GND.",
      "expected": "GND1 and GND2 should be on separate isolated ground nets to maintain galvanic isolation between the logic side and the CAN bus side.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ...)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation of the CAN transceivers is defeated, allowing ground loops and common-mode voltages to pass between the logic and bus sides, which can damage components and corrupt communication.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["R28", "R83", "SW5"],
      "pins": ["R28.1", "R28.2", "R83.1", "R83.2", "SW5.1", "SW5.2", "SW5.3", "SW5.4"],
      "nets": ["/NET0075", "/NET0078", "/NET0022", "/NET0209", "Net-(R28-Pad2)", "Net-(R83-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "R28 connects U24 CANL (/NET0075) to SW5 pin 1, which connects to SW5 pin 3 (U4 CANH /NET0209). R83 connects U4 CANL (/NET0078) to SW5 pin 2, which connects to SW5 pin 4 (U24 CANH /NET0022).",
      "expected": "R28 should connect U24 CANH to U24 CANL, and R83 should connect U4 CANH to U4 CANL, so that each 120R termination resistor is across its own CAN bus.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"195\") (name \"Net-(R28-Pad2)\") (node (ref \"R28\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"SW5\") (pin \"1\"))) ... (net (code \"197\") (name \"Net-(R83-Pad2)\") (node (ref \"R83\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"SW5\") (pin \"2\"))) ... (net (code \"9\") (name \"/NET0022\") ... (node (ref \"SW5\") (pin \"4\")) (node (ref \"U24\") (pin \"7\"))) ... (net (code \"46\") (name \"/NET0209\") ... (node (ref \"SW5\") (pin \"3\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"7\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "When termination is enabled via SW5, the two isolated CAN buses are connected through 120R resistors, bridging them and preventing proper termination of either bus, leading to communication errors.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_connection",
      "components": ["D45", "R34"],
      "pins": ["D45.2", "D45.4", "R34.1", "R34.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0102", "Net-(D45-K2)"],
      "observed": "D45 pin 4 (A2) is on NET0102; D45 pin 2 (K2) is on Net-(D45-K2); R34 is connected between Net-(D45-K2) and NET0102.",
      "expected": "R34 should connect Net-(D45-K2) to GND, so that the LED is in series with the current-limiting resistor to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"102\") (name \"NET0102\") ... (node (ref \"D45\") (pin \"4\")) (node (ref \"R34\") (pin \"2\"))) ... (net (code \"177\") (name \"Net-(D45-K2)\") (node (ref \"D45\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"R34\") (pin \"1\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The second LED in D45 will never illuminate because there is no path to ground; R34 is in parallel with the LED instead of in series, so the LED is effectively shorted and the resistor only loads the NET0102 signal.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: the isolated CAN transceivers have their isolated grounds tied together, the CAN termination resistors are cross-connected between the two buses, and a dual LED has its current-limiting resistor wired to the wrong net, preventing it from lighting."
}

